> I had a similar problem in my current game: I found a grey stone in a
> *chest*. How can I possibly test it without picking it up?

That one's easy if you have a wand of locking or know the wizard lock
spell (keys don't repair locks, magic does).

Carry the chest to a place with room on all sides. If it's very heavy,
that's already an indication that the stone inside is probably a
loadstone.

Lock the chest. While the lock is still whole you can use a key to avoid
wasting a wand charge.

#force with a blunt object (mace, staff, mattock). If you break open the
chest without destroying it, lock it and try again until you do destroy
it.

Now you've got your stone in the open to kick as you please.

